\name{MathOperators}
\alias{MathOperators}
\title{Arithmetic and rolling extremes an instrument calculates from its candle columns}
\description{
Each method fetches the instrument's candles through \code{prices()}, adds one or more columns and returns the candles. The class is a link in the chain of analysis classes that \code{Instrument} inherits, and \code{Instrument} supplies \code{prices()}.

The \code{talib} package has no arithmetic operators, no \code{MINMAX} and no index functions, and its \code{MAX} and \code{MIN} treat a missing value inside the data differently from Python's \code{talib}, so this class computes all of them in R. The arithmetic uses R's operators, which match TA-Lib's C code, and the rolling extremes and their positions follow TA-Lib 0.6.4's loops step by step.
}
